---
version: 2.0.2
title: testing: a module to lint that doesn't parse
file: ./test/grice/testing_test.gleam
test_name: a_module_to_lint_that_doesnt_parse_fails_the_run_test
---
error[grice/parse-error]: Can't parse this module
  ┌─ src/app.gleam:3:1
  │
3 │ }
  │ ^ glance didn't expect this

grice reads Gleam code with glance, and glance couldn't parse this file. No
rule ran on it, and the modules that import it may lose type information.

Hint: If `gleam build` accepts this file, glance doesn't support its syntax
yet, so please report it to glance.

A test over a module that doesn't parse would prove nothing, so the run
stops here. Fix the module, or exclude it in `gleam.toml` if the test needs
a linted module to import one that doesn't parse.

